<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Bbc-Micro on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/bbc-micro/</link><description>Recent content in Bbc-Micro on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/bbc-micro/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Retro Fractal Zoom</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/retro-fractal-zoom/</link><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/retro-fractal-zoom/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This one tickled my 8 bit brain.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I remember having to leave my BBC Micro on overnight to calculate a single low res image of a Mandelbrot fractal. Now, with a couple of prompts and a bit of to and fro with the Claude app on my phone, it renders a whole retro styled zoom video like this in a couple of minutes.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 0; position: relative; padding-bottom: 75%;"&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe style="width: 100%; height: 100%; position: absolute;" src="https://embedr.flickr.com/photos/55649516648" width="960" height="720" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowfullscreen title="Retro fractal zoom"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/55649516648/"&gt;Retro fractal zoom on Flickr&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Killer Gorilla on the BBC Micro</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/killer-gorilla-on-bbc-micro/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Jul 2016 12:18:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/killer-gorilla-on-bbc-micro/</guid><description>&lt;iframe allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="344" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/FoHKu9Q-f1I" width="459"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Not a bad attempt after 20 odd years of not playing.</description></item></channel></rss>